Falsifies `paging::domain::every_whole_page_of_the_grant_is_enumerated`.

The defect: the partial-page test is off by one, so the LAST whole page of every exactly-sized
grant is refused. `>=` reads right here (the offset plus a page must be inside the region), and
it is wrong for the same reason every half-open-interval off-by-one is wrong: `off + 4096 ==
size` means the page ends exactly at the end, which is inside.

This is the completeness direction, and it fails quietly in the direction that looks safe. The
device reaches less than it was granted, never more, so nothing about the confinement is
violated; the driver simply faults on the last page of its own DMA region, and the fault
arrives as an IOMMU translation failure rather than as anything naming this function. The
harness's header makes that argument already: a domain that mapped nothing at all would satisfy
soundness perfectly.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(grant_page(r, i), Some(iova), "a granted page is not the page its
own index enumerates")`, with `None` on the left, for the top page of any grant. The
`assert!(i < pages)` before it still passes, because `grant_pages` is untouched.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/domain.rs b/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
--- a/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ pub fn grant_pages(r: DmaRegion) -> Result<u64, MapError> {
 pub fn grant_page(r: DmaRegion, i: u64) -> Option<u64> {
     let off = i.checked_mul(PAGE_SIZE)?;
     // The whole page must fit: a trailing partial page is not one of the grant's pages.
-    if off.checked_add(PAGE_SIZE)? > r.size {
+    if off.checked_add(PAGE_SIZE)? >= r.size {
         return None;
     }
     r.base.checked_add(off)
